{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BringsSurface.EulerCharacteristicSix","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Matrix.Block","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":14,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant_dvd_X_pow_sub_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant_dvd_X_pow_sub_one","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L150-L162","doc":"`D_{2g}` divides `X^(2n) - 1` with `n = 2g + 1`. This is the algebraic core of \"the\nmonodromy of `T(2, n)` has order dividing `2n`\": Cayley–Hamilton turns it into `h^(2n) = 1`\nonce the characteristic polynomial of the monodromy is identified with `D_{2g}`, which is\nthe same determinant step left to the probe (it checks the order is exactly `2n` at\n`n = 3, 5, 7`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant_torus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant_torus","kind":"theorem","line":143,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L143-L147","doc":"For `T(2, 2g + 1)`: `(X + 1) · D_{2g} = X^(2g+1) + 1`, i.e. the Alexander polynomial\nis `(X^n + 1)/(X + 1)` with `n = 2g + 1` — degree `2g`, monic, as a fibered knot's must be. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant_mul_X_add_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant_mul_X_add_one","kind":"theorem","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L123-L140","doc":"`(X + 1) D_m = X^(m+1) + (-1)^m` for every `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.alexContinuant","kind":"def","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L115-L120","doc":"The continuant of `V - X·Vᵀ`: `D_0 = 1`, `D_1 = X - 1`,\n`D_{m+2} = (X - 1) D_{m+1} + X D_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.bennequin_genus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.bennequin_genus","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L101-L102","doc":"Bennequin genus `(c - k + 1) / 2` is `3` for both shapes — equal to `g(T(2,7))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.bennequin_chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.bennequin_chi","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L98-L99","doc":"Bennequin Euler characteristic `χ = k - c` for the two sub-braid shapes that occur. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.pages_embed_on_bring","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.pages_embed_on_bring","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L92-L96","doc":"The pages the probe found — `T(2,3)`, `T(2,5)`, `T(2,7)` — embed on Bring's surface at\nthe corpus's forced genus `4`, and `T(2,9)` is the last torus knot of this family that does. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:rem:torus-chain-pages-on-bring","label":"rem:torus-chain-pages-on-bring","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/torus-chain-pages-on-bring.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.bridge_bracket_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.bridge_bracket_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L86-L89","doc":"The braid presentation on `3A` strands gives `b ≤ 3A`, so the floor and the ceiling\nbracket `b` in `[2A + 1, 3A]`, which is non-empty exactly when `A ≥ 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.curvature_floor","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.curvature_floor","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L79-L84","doc":"**The curvature floor, as bookkeeping.** Granting Milnor (`inf ∫κ = 2π b`) and the\ncomponent-wise bridge bound `b ≥ μ + #knotted`, with `μ = A + 1` and `#knotted = A`, the\nfloor is `2π (2A + 1)`. Stated with the `2π` factored out. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:canonical-closure-torus-chain","label":"prop:canonical-closure-torus-chain","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/canonical-closure-torus-chain.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_det_three_five_seven","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_det_three_five_seven","kind":"theorem","line":73,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L73-L77","doc":"The three cases the probe checked, as instances. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_det_eq_one_of_even","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_det_eq_one_of_even","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L68-L71","doc":"For `T(2, n)` with `n` odd, `m = n - 1` is even and the Seifert form is unimodular\nwith determinant `1`: `H_1(page)` is self-dual under it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_det","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_det","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L63-L66","doc":"The Seifert matrix is upper triangular with `-1` down the diagonal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_blockTriangular","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2_blockTriangular","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L56-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.TorusKnotPages.seifertT2","kind":"def","line":51,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/TorusKnotPages.lean#L51-L54","doc":"Seifert matrix of `T(2, m + 1)` from its 2-strand positive braid: `m × m`, `-1` on\nthe diagonal, `+1` on the superdiagonal, `0` elsewhere. ","signatureChunk":0}]}